+// The projection is not in the binary: the game computes it and hands it to the vertex shader as four float4 rows in a
+// uniform buffer. It is found there by its perspective signature (the w row carries the -1 of the perspective, the first two
+// rows carry the x and y scales of the field of view, the off-diagonal terms are zero), and the aspect of those two scales has
+// to match the aspect of the game's own picture, which tells the camera's projection from a shadow map's.
+// The scaling is done on the host's own copy of the game's upload (the ring below), so the game and the GPU read the same
